{%- set marks = {'better': 'good', 'worse': 'bad', 'same': ''} -%}
{%- macro delta_class(d) %}{{ 'good' if d and d > 0 else ('bad' if d and d < 0 else '') }}{% endmacro -%}
{%- macro routes(side) %}{% for k, n in side.routed_to.items() %}<code>{{ k }}</code> {{ n }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% else %}–{% endfor %}{% endmacro -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Benchmark comparison {{ r.a.run_id }} vs {{ r.b.run_id }}</title>
{% include "_style.html.j2" %}
</head>
<body>
<main>
<p class="meta"><a href="../../index.html">← All runs</a></p>
<h1>{{ r.a.run_id }} vs {{ r.b.run_id }}</h1>
{% for key, s in (('A (baseline)', r.a), ('B', r.b)) %}
<p class="meta"><strong>{{ key }}</strong> <a href="../../{{ s.run_id }}/report.html">{{ side_name(s) }}</a>{% if s.agent_id %}, agent <code>{{ s.agent_id }}</code>{% endif %}{% if s.librechat is string %}, LibreChat <code>{{ s.librechat.split(':')[-1] }}</code>{% endif %} · judge <code>{{ s.judge_model }}</code> · {{ counts_text(s.counts) }}</p>
{% endfor %}
<p class="meta">{{ r.n_questions }} questions asked in both runs, repeats pooled{% if r.only_a %} · only in A: {{ r.only_a | join(', ') }}{% endif %}{% if r.only_b %} · only in B: {{ r.only_b | join(', ') }}{% endif %}</p>
{% if r.warnings %}
<div class="card warn">{% for w in r.warnings %}<p>⚠ {{ w }}</p>{% endfor %}</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Turns</h2>
<div class="card table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th></th><th>Expected</th><th>Completed</th><th>Failed</th><th>Missing</th><th>Ungraded</th><th>No reference</th><th>Eligible for recall</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for key, s in (('A', r.a), ('B', r.b)) %}{% set c = s.counts %}
    <tr><td>{{ key }}</td><td>{{ c.expected }}</td><td>{{ c.completed }}</td><td class="{{ 'bad' if c.failed }}">{{ c.failed }}</td><td class="{{ 'bad' if c.missing }}">{{ c.missing }}</td><td class="{{ 'bad' if c.ungraded }}">{{ c.ungraded }}</td><td>{{ c.no_reference }}</td><td>{{ c.eligible }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="note">A turn is one question × repeat. Failed: an HTTP error or timeout. Missing: never recorded. Eligible turns are the graded, failed and missing turns of questions with a reference; failed and missing ones count as not passed. Ungraded turns are left out of recall until they're graded.</p>

<h2>Headline</h2>
<div class="card table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>Δ (B − A)</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for m in r.metrics %}
    <tr><td>{{ m.label }}</td><td>{{ m.a | fmt(m.fmt) }}</td><td>{{ m.b | fmt(m.fmt) }}</td>
      <td class="{{ marks[m.verdict] }}">{{ m.delta | fmt(m.fmt, true) }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="note">Recall = passes / eligible turns = precision × attempt rate. Precision = passes / attempted answers (pass or fail, not declined). Attempt rate = attempted / eligible turns. The report-style pass rate (passes / graded answers) leaves failed turns out and is shown for continuity with the per-run reports. p90 is the value at sorted index ⌊0.9·n⌋ (the maximum for n ≤ 10). Per question (recall across repeats): <b>{{ r.question_verdicts.better }}</b> better, <b>{{ r.question_verdicts.worse }}</b> worse, {{ r.question_verdicts.same }} same. Green is better for B, red worse. Tool rounds and handoffs are only recorded in traces attached after the per-call trace change.</p>

<h2>Consistency across repeats</h2>
<div class="card table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Questions with mixed pass/fail across repeats</td><td>{{ r.a.consistency.flaky }}</td><td>{{ r.b.consistency.flaky }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mean per-question pass variance (0 = always agrees, 0.25 = coin flip)</td><td>{{ r.a.consistency.mean_pass_variance | fmt('num') }}</td><td>{{ r.b.consistency.mean_pass_variance | fmt('num') }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Median per-question latency stdev</td><td>{{ r.a.consistency.median_latency_stdev | fmt('secs') }}</td><td>{{ r.b.consistency.median_latency_stdev | fmt('secs') }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Routed to (agent that wrote the answer)</td><td>{{ routes(r.a) }}</td><td>{{ routes(r.b) }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

{% for title, rows in (('By category', r.by_category), ('By track', r.by_track)) %}
<h2>{{ title }}</h2>
<div class="card table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th></th><th>Completed / expected A</th><th>B</th><th>Failed · missing · ungraded A</th><th>B</th><th>Recall A</th><th>B</th><th>Δ</th><th>Precision A</th><th>B</th><th>Median A</th><th>B</th><th>p90 A</th><th>B</th><th>&lt;10s A</th><th>B</th><th>LLM calls A</th><th>B</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for c in rows %}
    <tr><td>{{ c.label }}</td><td>{{ c.a.completed }} / {{ c.a.expected }}</td><td>{{ c.b.completed }} / {{ c.b.expected }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.a.failed }} · {{ c.a.missing }} · {{ c.a.ungraded }}</td><td>{{ c.b.failed }} · {{ c.b.missing }} · {{ c.b.ungraded }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.a.recall | fmt('pct') }}</td><td>{{ c.b.recall | fmt('pct') }}</td>
      <td class="{{ delta_class(c.delta) }}">{{ c.delta | fmt('pct', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.a.precision | fmt('pct') }}</td><td>{{ c.b.precision | fmt('pct') }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.a.median_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td><td>{{ c.b.median_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.a.p90_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td><td>{{ c.b.p90_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.a.fast_share | fmt('pct') }}</td><td>{{ c.b.fast_share | fmt('pct') }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.a.mean_llm_calls | fmt('num') }}</td><td>{{ c.b.mean_llm_calls | fmt('num') }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endfor %}

<h2>Per question</h2>
<p class="note">Regressions first, then improvements, then unchanged. One mark per repeat: ✓ pass · ✗ fail · – declined · · no reference or ungraded · ! request failed · {{ missing_icon }} missing. “passes/eligible” after the marks. ⚠ marks a question asked or graded differently in A and B (compared only with --allow-mismatch).</p>
<div class="card table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Q</th><th>Category</th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>Δ recall</th><th>Precision A</th><th>B</th><th>F · M · U A</th><th>B</th><th>Median A</th><th>B</th><th>p90 A</th><th>B</th><th>&lt;10s A</th><th>B</th><th>Latency stdev B</th><th>LLM calls A</th><th>B</th><th>Routed to (B)</th><th>Question</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for q in r.questions %}
    <tr><td>{{ q.id }}</td><td>{{ q.category }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.a.icons }} {{ q.a.passes }}/{{ q.a.eligible }}</td><td>{{ q.b.icons }} {{ q.b.passes }}/{{ q.b.eligible }}</td>
      <td class="{{ marks[q.verdict] }}">{{ q.delta | fmt('pct', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.a.precision | fmt('pct') }}</td><td>{{ q.b.precision | fmt('pct') }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.a.failed }} · {{ q.a.missing }} · {{ q.a.ungraded }}</td><td>{{ q.b.failed }} · {{ q.b.missing }} · {{ q.b.ungraded }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.a.median_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td><td>{{ q.b.median_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.a.p90_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td><td>{{ q.b.p90_latency | fmt('secs') }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.a.fast_share | fmt('pct') }}</td><td>{{ q.b.fast_share | fmt('pct') }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.b.latency_stdev | fmt('secs') }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.a.mean_llm_calls | fmt('num') }}</td><td>{{ q.b.mean_llm_calls | fmt('num') }}</td>
      <td>{{ q.b.routed_to | join(', ') or '–' }}</td>
      <td class="text">{% if q.mismatch %}<span class="mismatch">⚠ changed: {{ q.mismatch | join(', ') }}</span> {% endif %}{{ q.question }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
</main>
</body>
</html>
